    "source": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md",
    "current_sha256": "be45e46699d9411cd96cd7bbced64693b0c3ccec7bc98aa3e76198ddbc08cddf",
    "original_sha256": "c4b012d163ec1e8623a51d57ad4ee561c4246aec837a2f6ae87a604407c1a042",
    "original_archive": "docs/evidence/empty-signature-receiving-831-20261016/before-2.txt",
    "edits": [
      {
        "new": "\n`canonical_shared/empty_signature.rs` owns the finite actual carrier census for\nempty canonical signatures. The lexical Exit branch authenticates the same\nheld receiver and zero-length signature vector, then inserts the real empty\nkey without a borrowed child query/Zip. The full immediate receiver remains\ncompiled in `before_empty_signature.rs`; wider paths and all original work,\npreflight and sticky failure rules remain intact. Qualification is pending.\n",
        "old": ""
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "source": "docs/FACTORED-SINGLETON-TARGETS-V1.md",
    "current_sha256": "720a89706b28fe4ff88739e05194468d6cd56b742d2f1ab19a223b2fb8db754b",
    "original_sha256": "3f2ae486cbaef9abf0167180fc2aedde47d4fcde6500257d58bf226214533566",
    "original_archive": "docs/evidence/empty-signature-receiving-831-20261016/before-3.txt",
    "edits": [
      {
        "new": "\n## Empty canonical signature receiving (source only)\n\nA canonical Exit with no successors retains its original signature-work debit,\npreflight, held payer authentication and insertion ordering. After explicit\nadmission of its actual branch and key constructors, it builds the real empty\nsignature directly. The original zero-length signature-vector authentication\nstill precedes dictionary lookup; signature insertion precedes state insertion.\nIt constructs no child-ID query, scratch-growth Result, child iterator or Zip.\nNo corresponding absent constructor is charged, and no old charge becomes a\ncredit. Nonempty signatures execute the complete existing borrowed-query path;\nthey also pay the actual new branch receivers, so unfavorable wide/unique cases\nmust remain visible. No weighted-state layout, graph identity, work ceiling,\nphysical cap or refusal authority changes.\n\nThe complete immediate d962 receiver remains independently compiled in\n`before_empty_signature.rs`, with all its ordinary/general branches intact.\nThe a82 log17 paid regression is historical: d962 already includes newer arena\nchanges, and its actual current gate outcome is pending. New tests compare\ncomplete IDs/states/six diagnostic fields/work frontiers, exact/short/zero paid\nlimits, sticky foreign/restored owner denial, actual heap/paid/peak and full\nDrop against that immediate receiver. The original strict paid gate and wide/\nunique controls remain unchanged. No executable gain or application recovery is\nclaimed before a fresh combined qualification.\n",
        "old": ""
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "source": "src/cleanup_plan/replay/factored/canonical_shared.rs",
    "current_sha256": "6568da26e2376af6e713fc396db3e9390907d8dedc7074c3dc314b76da348d6b",
    "original_sha256": "5a344d03d45d250d87e27b123f23b29ed4fae062f0d36ed5f4f8b166aca9de87",
    "original_archive": "docs/evidence/empty-signature-receiving-831-20261016/before-4.txt",
    "edits": [
      {
        "new": "                    // The old signature-work debit above remains first. Acquire\n                    // the actual new branch receivers before evaluating the guard.\n                    if budget.pays_allocations() {\n                        attempt!(budget.reserve_bytes(\n                            function, empty_signature::BRANCH_CONTROLS,\n                            \"canonical empty signature branch receiving\",\n                        ));\n                    }\n                    if successors.is_empty() {\n                        if budget.pays_allocations() {\n                            attempt!(budget.reserve_bytes(\n                                function, empty_signature::EMPTY_CONTROLS,\n                                \"canonical empty signature receiving\",\n                            ));\n                        }\n                        self.child_ids.clear();\n                        // Retain the original key-vector zero authentication;\n                        // no child directory, borrowed query or Zip exists here.\n                        attempt!(budget.reserve_array::<(Label, usize)>(\n                            function, 0, \"factored canonical signature vector\",\n                        ));\n                        let key = (accepted, Vec::new());\n                        let id = match self.ids.get(&key) {\n                            Some(id) => {\n                                #[cfg(test)]\n                                arena_tests::signature_lookup(true);\n                                *id\n                            }\n                            None => {\n                                #[cfg(test)]\n                                arena_tests::signature_lookup(false);\n                                intern_arena::prepare_insert!(self.ids, intern_arena::Signature, function, budget);\n                                let id = self.ids.len();\n                                self.ids.insert_prepaid(key, id);\n                                id\n                            }\n                        };\n                        self.child_ids.clear();\n                        if !self.states.contains_key(&state) {\n                            intern_arena::prepare_insert!(self.states, SharedWeighted, function, budget);\n                        }\n                        self.states.insert_prepaid(state, id);\n                        continue;\n                    }\n",
        "old": ""
      },
      {
        "new": "\nmod empty_signature;\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod before_empty_signature;\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod empty_signature_tests;\n",
        "old": ""
      }
    ]
  },
